SUMMARY:Concert: Marc Berger
DESCRIPTION:Presentation\n\nRIDE currently offers ten cinematic recordings 
 that capture the grandeur and allure of the West while examining its 
 profound origins in the American psyche. Marc and Mike Ricciardi created 
 the album\, which is based on Marc's lifelong love affair with the American 
 West. "Twister" has a melancholy message and beat\, "Take It on the Chin" 
 is about taming a wild horse\, "Time Waits For No Man" is about a sexy\, 
 mind-blowing encounter in the middle of nowhere\, and seven more scenic 
 stops make up RIDE's Great American Frontier tour.\n\n \n\nAbout the 
 artist\n\nMarc's life revolves around two passions: composing and 
 performing original songs and touring the American West. At SXSW Music 
 Festival and Kerrville Folk Festival\, he has opened for big stars like Bob 
 Dylan and sang his antinuclear hymn "The Last One\," a mainstay of Richie 
 Havens' shows.
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Performance
