SUMMARY:Buena Vista Social Club: The musical
DESCRIPTION:Learn about the fascinating history of the Buena Vista Social 
 Club -- the band and the musical -- in this lecture by Rick 
 Feingold.\n\nProgram\n\nBefore the revolution altered the course of Cuban 
 music\, a band of young musicians in Havana in the 1950s had already begun 
 to shake things up. In a surprising twist\, the band reunited forty years 
 later to record the songs they had left behind\, and the result was the 
 best-selling album in the history of world music. Years later\, the band 
 would become the subject of a Tony-winning Broadway musical. Feingold's 
 presentation will focus on the musical and include clips from the 1999 
 documentary film Son Cubano\, as well as discussion of life in Cuba in the 
 1950s before the revolution.\n\nPresenter\n\nRick Feingold oversaw the 
 Latin Jazz series at the Performing Arts Center at Penn State University. 
 In addition to extensive travels throughout Cuba\, Feingold teaches history 
 at Bergen Community College. Mr. Feingold has a Bachelor of Arts in History 
 from Rutgers University and an MBA from Penn State University.
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Lecture
UID:LibCal-10341-16773371
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16773371
