BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260927T180000Z
DTEND:20260927T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20260927T000000Z
SUMMARY:Lenore Raphael Trio performs Jazz standards
DESCRIPTION:Program\n\nThe Lenore Raphael Trio consists of Lenore on 
 piano\, Hilliard Greene on bass\, and Kahlil Kwame Bell on drums\, creating 
 a world-class ensemble. Their performance will feature jazz classics and 
 selections from the American songbook.\n\n \n\nArtist\n\nLenore Raphael is 
 a jazz pianist\, radio personality\, Steinway artist\, and jazz educator 
 who is widely considered to be among the top pianists working in modern 
 music. Major jazz clubs and festivals have sold out her performances on 
 multiple occasions. New York City's Birdland\, The Blue Note\, and Jazz at 
 Lincoln Center were all stops for Dizzy's\, and among them are the 
 following: the Ottawa International Jazz Festival\, Ronnie Scott's in 
 London\, the S.S. Oosterdam jazz cruise\, the Tel Aviv Jazz Festival\, and 
 multiple others. The Joy Of Jazz event in Johannesburg\, South Africa\, 
 featured three internationally known Steinway pianists\, including Abdullah 
 Ibraham and Ahmad Jamal. She was one of them. Additionally\, in April 
 2014\, Lenore played to sold-out crowds at the Broward Center for the Arts 
 Amaturo theater in Ft. Lauderdale\, Florida\, and the Casa Da Musica in 
 Porto\, Portugal. England\, Europe\, and Israel have all been stops on her 
 tour. She had a giant tour in South Africa in 2016\, and every place she 
 played there requested her to come back.\n\n
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Performance
UID:LibCal-10341-16402849
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16402849
END:VEVENT
